From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:55:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Link the REAL*16 check with LDFLAGS

The check has to run the executable it builds. When cross-compiling the
executable is run under emulation, where without the rpath from LDFLAGS
libgfortran is not found. The check then reports no REAL*16 support and
the library is silently built with RealQuad as double precision.
---
 configure | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 1200bee..3c56eb0 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -281,7 +281,7 @@ tee $test.f << _EOF_ 1>&2
 	end
 _EOF_
 
-eval $CONF_FC$CONF_FFLAGS -o $test$CONF_EXE $test.f 1>&2
+eval $CONF_FC$CONF_FFLAGS -o $test$CONF_EXE $test.f $CONF_LDFLAGS 1>&2
 
 ./$test$CONF_EXE 1>&2 && {
   echo "yes" 1>&3
